#!/bin/bash

# tam-menu-keybindings — search the desktop's keybindings and run the chosen
# one (Menu → Learn → Keybindings, SUPER + K).
#
#   tam-menu-keybindings [--print|-p]
#
# --print writes the list to stdout instead of opening the menu.
#
# Ported from Omarchy 4.0.4 (omarchy-menu-keybindings) for plan 18 0.2.2.
# Changed: the rows come from the Tamlinux shell's keybindings service, which
# reads the compositor facade's bindings; this script keeps the Lua command
# scan and the dispatch, so Enter runs the binding's command. Both are
# Hyprland-only. The menu is tam-menu-select.
